course: dictionary
lesson: 15376
title: Spasm: a sudden tightening or burst
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spasm is a sudden tightening of a muscle that you cannot control, and it may hurt. «Maya felt a spasm in her calf halfway through the race.» Her leg tightened all at once and she could not stop it, so spasm means a sudden, uncontrolled squeeze.
explain: The word can also mean a sudden short burst of a feeling or action. «She gave a spasm of laughter at the joke.» The laugh came in one quick burst, not as a long, steady giggle. Ask yourself: is this a body thing that hurts, or a sudden burst of feeling?
explain: In PE you may hear that a muscle can go into spasm when you are tired or have not warmed up. Stretching helps. «Jack's back went into spasm when he bent to tie his laces.» To check your meaning, swap in "sudden tightening" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Spasm is a noun: one spasm, two spasms.
fact: «Spasm» means a sudden tightening of a muscle that you cannot control, which may hurt.
fact: «Spasm» can also mean a sudden short burst of a feeling or action, like «a spasm of anger».
fact: Useful phrases are «back spasm» and «go into spasm».
fact: Tiredness and not warming up can make a muscle spasm, and stretching can help.
exercise: What is a spasm in a muscle? | *A sudden tightening of a muscle that you cannot control | A slow, gentle stretch | A cold drink after running | A long nap
exercise: «She gave a spasm of laughter at the joke.» What does spasm mean here? | A cough from a cold | *A sudden short burst of laughter | A long, quiet giggle | A sore leg
exercise: Which can help stop a muscle spasm during PE? | *Stretching and warming up | Sitting still for an hour | Eating a big meal just before | Running backwards
test: «Tom's back went into spasm when he lifted the bag.» What does go into spasm mean? | *His back muscle tightened suddenly and he could not control it | A new bag was given to his back | He stood up very straight on purpose | His back felt cold
test: «A spasm of fear ran through the little girl as the lights went out.» What is a spasm of fear? | A long, calm feeling | *A sudden short rush of fear | A gift from a friend | A toy she lost
exam: Which sentence uses spasm to mean a sudden short burst of feeling? | She walked to school with a spasm | *A spasm of anger made her slam the door | The muscle felt sore and stiff | The doctor checked his leg
